web888-websdr (2026.730-2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Step 3.5 Debian compatibility fixes
    (step 3, WebSDR Debian fixes):
    - 0014: admin network page writes a staged ifupdown drop-in via the
      sudo root helper instead of rewriting /etc/network/interfaces
      (brick risk on Debian); lbu commit and direct /etc writes stay
      Alpine-only behind a runtime distro check.
    - 0015: reboot/halt/poweroff call the web888-poweroff root helper.
    - 0016: websdr root-password auto-hardening is Alpine-only now
      (image layer owns the root password).
  * Ship /etc/sudoers.d/web888 (mode 0440, postinst visudo -c) granting
    user web888 NOPASSWD on exactly the two root-owned helper scripts
    in /usr/lib/web888/root-helpers/.
  * Unit: +CAP_NET_ADMIN (KIWI iptables chain), +DeviceAllow
    ttyUSB*/ttyACM* (CAT serial), +ReadWritePaths for the two helper
    target paths; NoNewPrivileges removed (sudo is setuid — NNP blocks
    the root-helper mechanism entirely).
  * Depends += iptables, miniupnpc, netcat-openbsd, sudo.

